{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj3jmZYqWUB3dktf4CpT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. The mechanism engages.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand before you — heavy oak, iron-banded, ancient. My grain tells centuries. My hinges have sung for kings and for no one. The cold of my handle waits for your palm.\n\nI am locked now.\n\nWhat stands on the other side, I will not say. That is not my nature. I hold the threshold. I divide here from there, known from unknown, safe from unsafe.\n\nYou may knock.\nYou may turn away.\nYou may find the key.\n\nBut I do not open for words alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":143,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}